'''Actæa''' (ak-tē′ä̤), ''n.'' [L., herb-christopher, from the resemblance of the leaves to those of the
[[FIGURE]]
{{c|{{smaller|Red Baneberry (''Actæa rubra''), showing flowering plant and fruiting raceme.}}}}
elder, < Gr. ἀκταία, erroneous form of ἀκτέα, contr. ἀκτῆ, the elder-tree.] A genus of herbs, natural order ''Ranunculaceæ'', with somewhat deleterious properties. {{smaller|The old-world species, ''A. spicata'', the baneberry or herb-christopher, has black berries. The common forms of North America with red berries are now considered varieties of the same species, but the white-berried ''A.''}}

